 "dur": 45.0,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Wanda's flat-bottomed soda cans waddled off the shelf like penguins.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.682
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Flat is fancy!\" said Wanda, boss of Fizzwell Soda. So why do real cans have a dent underneath?",
   "s": 3.882,
   "e": 8.882
  },
  {
   "text": "By lunch, every flat bottom had puffed into a round belly.",
   "s": 9.182,
   "e": 11.964
  },
  {
   "text": "Pogo, the factory dog, was thrilled. Rolling cans meant fetch. Six hundred rounds of fetch.",
   "s": 12.164,
   "e": 17.113
  },
  {
   "text": "So Wanda made the metal twice as thick. \"Flat is fancy!\"",
   "s": 17.313,
   "e": 20.254
  },
  {
   "text": "Now each can weighed as much as a brick. The delivery truck sat down like a tired camel.",
   "s": 20.374,
   "e": 24.905
  },
  {
   "text": "Then a hot day hit, and two hundred bellies popped at once. Soda rained from the ceiling.",
   "s": 25.105,
   "e": 28.92
  },
  {
   "text": "So why the dent?",
   "s": 29.12,
   "e": 29.864
  },
  {
   "text": "Fizz pushes out hard on every part of the can. A flat bottom bends.",
   "s": 30.164,
   "e": 33.644
  },
  {
   "text": "A dome pushes back like an arch, so thin metal can hold the fizz.",
   "s": 34.044,
   "e": 37.343
  },
  {
   "text": "Wanda brought the dent back. Pogo kept one belly can as his ball.",
   "s": 37.543,
   "e": 40.951
  },
  {
   "text": "\"Flat is fancy,\" Wanda says now. About her hat.",
   "s": 41.151,
   "e": 43.4
  }
 ],
